    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our primary target with a 72.82 score. His favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker is amplified by a strong park factor and a solid projection in the #5 hole, making him our highest-ceiling asset. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** earns a \"Strong\" designation (70.47) despite a challenging matchup against Bassitt; the math favors him heavily today due to a positive platoon edge and his high-leverage spot in the #2 order position. While **Gleyber Torres** and **Zack Gelof** both provide respectable mid-60s to high-50s production, the core of our offense relies on these two capitalizing on their respective situational advantages to keep our Roto standings afloat.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Braden Montgomery**, whose score of 39.41 narrowly missed our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. While he offers some positional flexibility, the matchup against the tougher arm of Jobe suppressed his upside enough to keep him on the pine. We are exercising caution with **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Zack Gelof**, as both are playing in lineups that are currently \"Pending.\" While we have modeled them under the assumption of favorable top-of-the-order placement, any shift in their batting position could significantly alter their daily efficiency. Furthermore, while we monitor **Cal Raleigh**, his score of 54.46 reflects a conservative outlook; his lower-third placement in the order combined with the defensive tax of the catcher position makes him a marginal start that we are relying on for secondary power rather than elite output.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the scarcity of stolen bases. **Masyn Winn**, while starting today, carries a \"Below Floor\" risk regarding his speed-based efficiency\u2014his current output is dampened by the high-quality, high-hold environment against Holmes, which historically stifles SB opportunities. We are holding **Justin Crawford** in reserve for better conditions, and with **Will Smith** still sidelined, we are stretching our depth thin. Keep a close watch on the weather and official lineups; if **Lawrence Butler** or **Jung Hoo Lee** are shuffled down in their respective orders, we may see their scores dip below our comfort threshold, necessitating a pivot to our bench depth.",
